\title{Ordinary and singular points}
\taxon{Definition}
\date{2021-10-01}
\author{JB00}
\import{macros}

\p{A point #{x_0} is an \em{ordinary point} of (#{\ast}) if both #{\frac{q(x)}{p(x)}} and #{\frac{r(x)}{p(x)}} have Taylor series around #{x_0} (“analytic” there). Otherwise, it is a \em{singular point}.}
